course: dictionary
lesson: 3330
title: Evergreen: always green
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An evergreen tree keeps its green leaves all year round. Look at the word: ever means always, and green is a colour, so evergreen means always green. «Evergreen trees keep leaves all year and lose old ones little by little.» The clue is inside the word.
explain: Read the sentence around the word. «Thin needles with a waxy coat help evergreen trees lose little water in winter.» Pines and firs have needles, and they stay green in winter. Ask: what would fit in «Evergreen trees keep their needles all year»? Your meaning fits, so you are right.
explain: Evergreen can also describe a song or film that stays popular for a long time. The tree idea still works: the song does not fade, just as the tree keeps its green. Check the sentence to see which meaning the author uses.
fact: Evergreen (adjective) means keeping green leaves or needles all year round.
fact: An evergreen (noun) is a tree or bush such as a pine, holly or fir.
fact: «Deciduous» trees, like oak, maple and birch, drop their leaves in autumn, while «evergreen» trees keep theirs.
fact: Pines, firs and spruces have needles and are evergreen; most eucalyptus trees in Australia are evergreen too.
fact: «Evergreen» can also mean something that stays popular for a long time, like «an evergreen song».
exercise: «Evergreen trees keep leaves all year.» What does evergreen mean? | Very tall and thin | *Keeping green leaves all year round | Growing only in summer | Losing all their leaves in autumn
exercise: Which of these trees is evergreen? | Maple | *Pine | Birch | Oak
exercise: In the phrase «an evergreen song», what does evergreen mean? | A very loud song | *Something that stays popular for a long time | A song about trees losing their leaves | A song sung in a forest
test: Which tree in this list keeps its needles all year? | Birch | Maple | Oak | *Spruce
test: Mia says, «Deciduous trees drop their leaves in autumn.» Which word is the opposite of evergreen? | Green | Holly | *Deciduous | Ancient
exam: «Evergreen trees keep their needles all year, while deciduous trees rest in winter.» Why are pines called evergreen? | Because they are very old | Because they drop their leaves in autumn | *Because they keep their green needles all year | Because they grow only in summer
